{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"3332","artifact_type":"architect","name":"plan/architect-docs-backlog-item-groomed-schema-field-drift.md@sha256:afa7cf82763f1162f36a3fd76679081f478faec0f6ce269e883c969087771bd3"},"owner_reference":"3332","content":"# Architect Spec \u2014 #3332: `docs/backlog-item-groomed-schema.md` field drift\n\n**Target file**: `plugins/development-harness/docs/backlog-item-groomed-schema.md`\n**Scope**: Text corrections only, six edit sites, no other file touched. This is a documentation-accuracy fix \u2014 no code, no interfaces, no new abstractions. Each item below is a precise before/after text specification for the implementing task to apply verbatim (adapted only for surrounding punctuation/line wrap, not content).\n\nAll line numbers below are the **current** (pre-edit) numbers, confirmed by direct read of the file at HEAD in this worktree. Per R4 (feature-context \u00a74), applying these edits will shift line numbers below `:11`; `docs/workflow-layers/KNOWN_ENTITIES.md:314`/`:357` cites this file's `## Groomed Sections` table as `L64\u201381` \u2014 that citation should be spot-checked after the edit lands, but re-verifying/fixing it is **out of scope** for this item (AC: \"No other file changes are introduced\").\n\n---\n\n## Edit 1 \u2014 Frontmatter `name:` field (line 15)\n\n**Current:**\n```yaml\nname: \"Item title\"\n```\n\n**Corrected:**\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Item title\"\n```\n\n**Citation:** `backlog_core/models.py:1011-1013` \u2014 `BacklogItem` defines `title: str = \"\"`, `reference: str = \"\"`, `description: str = \"\"`. There is no `name` field on `BacklogItem` or `BacklogItemMetadata`.\n\n**Note (resolves feature-context Q1):** Do not add a sentence documenting `name` as a legacy read-time alias (`parsing.py:363` accepts it on read for backward compatibility with old files, never writes it). This doc instructs what the groomer *writes*; the alias is a read-time compatibility shim for files that predate this schema, not part of the schema being defined. Mentioning it would reintroduce exactly the ambiguity the fix removes \u2014 keep the frontmatter example to real, current, write-time fields only.\n\n**Note on `reference`:** `BacklogItem.reference` is not added to the frontmatter example. It is not among the AC's required checks, and `models.py:1000-1008`'s docstring describes it as an internally-managed collision-detection field (title-hash fallback), not something an authoring agent sets by hand. Adding it would be scope creep beyond what AC #1/#2 require; leave the example as `title` + `description` + `metadata:` block, matching current structure minus the `name`\u2192`title` rename.\n\n---\n\n## Edit 2 \u2014 \"Location\" framing (line 5)\n\n**Current:**\n```\n**Location**: Groomed content lives in the **body** of `~/.dh/projects/{slug}/backlog/{priority}-{slug}.md` (resolved via `dh_paths.backlog_dir()`). Frontmatter uses the research-style `metadata:` block (aligned with `./research/` entries). Body has no duplication of frontmatter \u2014 only extra fields when present, plus `## Groomed` when groomed.\n```\n\n**Corrected:**\n```\n**Scope**: This document defines the groomed *content* schema \u2014 frontmatter shape, body sections, and `## Groomed` subsections \u2014 passed through `backlog_groom(groomed_content=...)`. This content is identical regardless of which backend (github, sqlite, memory, beads) stores it; physical storage format and location are backend internals (see `AGENTS.md` \u00a7Backend Providers) and are out of scope here. Frontmatter uses the research-style `metadata:` block (aligned with `./research/` entries). Body has no duplication of frontmatter \u2014 only extra fields when present, plus `## Groomed` when groomed.\n```\n\n**Citation:**\n- `backlog_core/yaml_io.py:87` \u2014 `save_item()` docstring: \"Always writes `.yaml` format regardless of the original file extension\" (the doc's hardcoded `.md` path is stale even for the one backend it describes).\n- `AGENTS.md:538-565` (plugin-level, `plugins/development-harness/AGENTS.md`) \u00a7Backend Providers \u2014 four backend families (`github`, `sqlite`, `memory`, `beads`); \"Beads, SQLite, and Memory use native storage directly and never read/write backlog YAML or instantiate `FileCache`\" (`:562-563`). The per-item-file path structure the doc asserts exists only for GitHub's local cache.\n- Same file, \u00a7State Management (`:91` and surrounding) \u2014 \"Physical paths, cache records, provider IDs, and wire formats are backend internals\" (design-intent citation, feature-context \u00a75).\n\n**Structural implication (resolves feature-context Q2, R3):** AC #4 permits either a universal-true statement or an explicitly-scoped backend-specific one. This spec chooses **replace \"Location\" with \"Scope\", and state the content/storage boundary explicitly** rather than trying to write one storage sentence that's true for all four backends \u2014 no such single sentence exists (three backends have no file-path concept at all). This also directly implements the Design Intent Alignment finding (feature-context \u00a75): physical storage is a backend internal an agent-facing doc should not assert. The replacement is the same length as the original (one paragraph, no section added or removed) \u2014 no knock-on restructuring of the surrounding `# Backlog Item Groomed Schema` intro block (lines 1-7) is needed.\n\n---\n\n## Edit 3 \u2014 Status vocabulary example (line 23)\n\n**Current:**\n```yaml\nstatus: open|in-progress|done|resolved\n```\n\n**Corrected:**\n```yaml\nstatus: open|done|in-progress|needs-grooming|closed\n```\n\n**Citation:** `backlog_core/models.py:723` \u2014 `_VALID_STATUSES = {\"open\", \"done\", \"in-progress\", \"needs-grooming\", \"closed\"}`. The doc's `resolved` is not canonical (`models.py:882-896`'s `_validate_status` preserves `resolved` only as a legacy read-time value, same category as the `name` alias in Edit 1); the doc also omits `needs-grooming` and `closed` entirely.\n\n---\n\n## Edit 4 \u2014 Prose rule's `name` reference (line 46)\n\n**Current:**\n```\nDo **not** duplicate `name`, `description`, `source`, `added`, `priority`, `type`, `issue` in the body \u2014 they live in frontmatter.\n```\n\n**Corrected:**\n```\nDo **not** duplicate `title`, `description`, `source`, `added`, `priority`, `type`, `issue` in the body \u2014 they live in frontmatter.\n```\n\n**Citation:** Same as Edit 1 (`backlog_core/models.py:1011-1013`) \u2014 this is the second occurrence of the identical `name`\u2192`title` drift (feature-context Concern C1). Both occurrences must change together or the doc is left internally inconsistent \u2014 one line says `title` in frontmatter, the other still says `name` is the field to avoid duplicating.\n\n---\n\n## Edit 5 \u2014 Priority vocabulary example (line 21)\n\n**Current:**\n```yaml\npriority: P0|P1|P2|Ideas\n```\n\n**Corrected:**\n```yaml\npriority: P0|P1|P2|Ideas|completed\n```\n\n**Citation:** `backlog_core/models.py:721` \u2014 `_VALID_PRIORITIES = {\"P0\", \"P1\", \"P2\", \"Ideas\", \"completed\"}` (verified directly at that line in this worktree). The doc omits `completed`.\n\n**Note (concern flagged to team lead, not blocking):** `models.py:733-739`'s `VALID_NEW_ITEM_PRIORITIES` deliberately **excludes** `completed` from the set a caller may request when creating a new item \u2014 the comment there states `completed` \"is populated internally when an item transitions to a completed state, never something a caller creating a NEW item should be able to request directly.\" Listing `priority: P0|P1|P2|Ideas|completed` flat, with no annotation, risks teaching the groomer agent that `completed` is a value it may freely write \u2014 the same class of error (an internal/derived value presented as an authoring choice) as the defect this item fixes for `resolved` status and `name`. Recommend the implementing task append a short parenthetical: `priority: P0|P1|P2|Ideas|completed  # \"completed\" is set internally on completion, not chosen by the groomer`. This stays within AC #5's literal requirement (exact match to `_VALID_PRIORITIES`, no missing canonical value) while not reintroducing an authoring-ambiguity regression. If the team prefers strict minimalism (AC's wording asks only for vocabulary match, not an annotation), the bare corrected line above also satisfies the AC as written \u2014 this is a judgment call for the implementer, not a blocking requirement.\n\n---\n\n## Edit 6 \u2014 Broken relative link (line 11)\n\n**Current:**\n```markdown\nAligned with [research/README.md](../../research/README.md) metadata format:\n```\n\n**Corrected:**\n```markdown\nAligned with [research/README.md](../../../research/README.md) metadata format:\n```\n\n**Citation:** The doc lives at `plugins/development-harness/docs/backlog-item-groomed-schema.md`. Resolving `../../` from that location reaches `plugins/` \u2014 `plugins/research/README.md` does not exist (confirmed absent). Resolving `../../../` reaches the repo root \u2014 `research/README.md` exists there (confirmed present at HEAD in this worktree). One additional `../` is required: `docs/` \u2192 `development-harness/` \u2192 `plugins/` \u2192 repo root is three levels, not two.\n\n**Scope note:** The `metadata:` block nesting shown in the frontmatter example (lines 17-30) is itself correct \u2014 `BacklogItem.metadata: BacklogItemMetadata` is real (`models.py:1018`) \u2014 this edit touches only the link path, nothing else in that block.\n\n---\n\n## Summary of all line-15/21/23/46 changes to the frontmatter block (lines 13-32)\n\nFor implementer convenience, the frontmatter code fence (currently lines 13-32) after Edits 1, 3, 5 applied together:\n\n```yaml\n---\ntitle: \"Item title\"\ndescription: \"Main problem statement or description\"\nmetadata:\n  topic: \"slug-from-title\"\n  source: \"Source description\"\n  added: \"YYYY-MM-DD\"\n  priority: P0|P1|P2|Ideas|completed\n  type: Feature|Bug|Refactor|Docs|Chore\n  status: open|done|in-progress|needs-grooming|closed\n  # optional:\n  issue: \"#N\"\n  plan: \"path/to/plan.md\"\n  groomed: \"YYYY-MM-DD\"\n  layer: \"0\"|\"1\"|\"2\"\n  language: python|typescript|...\n  stack: fastapi|python-cli|...\n---\n```\n\n(`type: Feature|Bug|Refactor|Docs|Chore` at line 22 was verified against `_VALID_TYPES` in `models.py:722` and is already correct \u2014 no change.)\n\n---\n\n## Explicitly out of scope (per AC \"No other file changes are introduced\")\n\n- `plugins/development-harness/templates/backlog-item.md`'s identical `name:`/`title` drift (feature-context R2) \u2014 separate follow-up item, not this diff.\n- The `## Groomed` section inventory (lines 62-81) \u2014 already reconciled against `section_registry.py` by #2979, no drift found, not touched here.\n- The \"No line numbers\" rule at line 58, which contradicts how #3332 itself was groomed (feature-context Concern C2) \u2014 flagged, not fixed here.\n- The unversioned \"When groomed after Issue #314\" condition at line 80 (Concern C3) \u2014 flagged, not fixed here.\n- Re-verifying/updating `KNOWN_ENTITIES.md:314`/`:357`'s `L64\u201381` line-range citation after this edit shifts line numbers (R4) \u2014 a follow-up spot-check, not part of this diff.\n\n---\n\n## Verification performed for this spec\n\nAll citations in this document were independently re-verified by direct file read at HEAD in this worktree (not taken solely from upstream grooming output):\n\n- `backlog_core/models.py:721` \u2192 `_VALID_PRIORITIES = {\"P0\", \"P1\", \"P2\", \"Ideas\", \"completed\"}` \u2014 confirmed.\n- `backlog_core/models.py:722` \u2192 `_VALID_TYPES = {\"Feature\", \"Bug\", \"Refactor\", \"Docs\", \"Chore\"}` \u2014 confirmed, matches doc, no change needed.\n- `backlog_core/models.py:723` \u2192 `_VALID_STATUSES = {\"open\", \"done\", \"in-progress\", \"needs-grooming\", \"closed\"}` \u2014 confirmed.\n- `backlog_core/models.py:733-739` \u2192 `VALID_NEW_ITEM_PRIORITIES` excludes `completed` by design \u2014 confirmed, informs the Edit 5 annotation note.\n- `backlog_core/models.py:1011-1013` \u2192 `BacklogItem.title`/`reference`/`description` \u2014 confirmed.\n- `backlog_core/yaml_io.py:87` \u2192 `save_item()` docstring \"Always writes `.yaml` format...\" \u2014 confirmed (line 84 is `def save_item(...)`, line 87 is the cited docstring line).\n- `AGENTS.md:538-565` \u2192 \u00a7Backend Providers, four backend families, native-storage-only backends never read/write backlog YAML \u2014 confirmed. Note: this section lives in the **plugin-level** `AGENTS.md` (`plugins/development-harness/AGENTS.md`), not the repo-root `AGENTS.md` \u2014 the corrected doc text should cite the plugin-level path if the citation is made explicit, to avoid a fresh drift point.\n- `research/README.md` (repo root) exists; `plugins/research/README.md` does not \u2014 confirmed via direct filesystem check.\n\n## Post-Implementation Annotations\n\nAdded by context-refinement agent on 2026-08-31\n\n### Design Refinements\n\n1. Single-file AC #6 is unsatisfiable under the repo's auto-sync-manifests pre-commit hook: implementation and independent quality-gate review both confirm the landed commit touches the target doc plus three plugin.json manifests bumped by `plugins/development-harness/.pre-commit-config.yaml:160-166` (`files: ^plugins/`, `pass_filenames: false`) \u2014 a repo-wide, unconditional side effect, not implementer error. The same three-file bump pattern appears on the two commits immediately preceding this one in git history.\n   - Original: \"No other file changes are introduced\" (item AC #6, quoted in plan P74e3c201's acceptance criteria for T1/T2).\n   - Actual: commit modifies 4 files \u2014 the target doc plus `.claude-plugin/plugin.json`, `.codex-plugin/plugin.json`, `.cursor-plugin/plugin.json`.\n   - Recorded in: P74e3c201/T2 (GAPS_FOUND verdict), independently reproduced in quality-gate code-review artifact `code-review-T1-qg-docs-backlog-item-groomed-schema-field-drift`.\n   - Note: No `Intent Source` reference is present on this artifact (pre-policy artifact), so this is classified design-refinement per the context-refinement policy default rather than intent-divergence, despite the divergence-threshold table's literal \"constraint violated\" language.\n\n2. Edit 2's replacement text (line 5) introduced a new, previously-absent factual claim that is itself inaccurate: \"passed through `backlog_groom(groomed_content=...)`\" \u2014 `backlog_groom()` has no `groomed_content` parameter (`backlog_core/server.py:2550-2616` defines `selector`, `section`, `content`, `entry_id`, `replace_section`, `reason`, `append`, `sections`, `mark_groomed` instead). T1 applied this spec's Edit 2 text verbatim as instructed; the inaccuracy originates in this architect spec, not in an implementation deviation from it.\n   - Original architect spec text (Edit 2, corrected block, above): \"...frontmatter shape, body sections, and `## Groomed` subsections \u2014 passed through `backlog_groom(groomed_content=...)`...\"\n   - Actual: no such parameter exists; correct framing is `backlog_groom(selector=..., section=..., content=...)`.\n   - Recorded in: `doc-drift-audit-backlog-item-groomed-schema` artifact (2026-08-31), independent of this plan's own T1/T2 tasks.\n   - Action needed: A follow-up fix to `plugins/development-harness/docs/backlog-item-groomed-schema.md` line 5 is required to correct the `backlog_groom()` reference; not blocking for this item's own nine ACs (none of which named the function-signature claim) but is an active drift as of this annotation.\n"}